From f8c6f5bbc2a36c20c4da3620a8e104c32c2d46e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:53:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] metrics: Prometheus /metrics with lock-free recording
 (first metrics)

Operators want to scrape the node with Prometheus. -metrics (default
off) serves /metrics in the Prometheus text format (0.0.4) on the RPC
listeners. It is an ordinary HTTP handler, so it gets RPC's access
rules: only -rpcallowip clients (the address resolved through
-trustedproxy), never -publicbind listeners. It has no authentication,
as scrapers expect, which is why it is opt-in: an -rpcallowip opened for
authenticated RPC does not start publishing node state.

Recording must not slow validation or P2P, so it takes no lock, makes
no allocation and no system call (src/metrics):

- Counters are split into 16 cache-line aligned shards; a thread adds to
  its own with a relaxed fetch_add and the shards are summed when
  scraped. Eight threads on one counter cost 2.3 ns per add, against 45
  ns for a single shared atomic.
- Event histograms (durations, sizes) go through a bounded single
  producer ring per recording thread (6 ns per sample). A full ring drops
  the sample and counts it (lotus_metrics_dropped_samples_total); a drain
  thread folds the rings into fixed buckets every 50 ms. Rings of exited
  threads are drained once more and freed.
- Gauges are single relaxed atomics, set where a value changes.
- With -metrics off, a recording site is one load and a branch.

Scrapes drain and render on an HTTP worker under the registry's own
locks, which recording never takes; a rendering is reused for 1 s.

This first set is lotus_p2p_received_bytes_total{type} (recorded at the
existing per-message-type accounting) and lotus_block_connect_seconds
(around ConnectBlock). Further metrics follow the design under review
(mirrored chain/mempool/peer gauges, RPC and HTTP latencies).
